{"parentUuid":"a2e97bf5-2275-4874-8db3-b95f1110559e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"50b0f09b-314b-4bce-88c1-683a5cd802dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AoCLEFzPzeeKMxQdPZSTWb","type":"tool_result","content":"[entire] Pushing 3 checkpoint ref(s) to origin................................................................ done\nee4435e A5 live exit: rules bind words in order, push handlers stop with their page","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b6c23873-1839-4aa1-82a6-9ef8f96f2019","timestamp":"2026-10-31T15:22:09.452Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"[entire] Pushing 3 checkpoint ref(s) to origin................................................................ done\nee4435e A5 live exit: rules bind words in order, push handlers stop with their page","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":648,"oldLines":7,"newStart":648,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | A2 | done | The console on the Engine page: containers with versions, state, stop, start and live logs; functions and trigger types with a filter; queues with depth, delivered, failed and dead letters. One `console` read through the Engine seam, 23 tests. Live exit (2026-10-30): `judge` stopped and started from the window, a stop made from the CLI reached the page by push with no reload, and its logs streamed. `ade` was removed with `compose::remove` (23 containers), so nothing in the stack serves HTTP. |"," | A3 | done | `bastion-core` (9caf363), the Store (93b5cb8), spike N7 (c640769), the factory loop (88f45fb), and the first views (778016d), with fixes from the exit. 28 app tests and 15 core tests pass. Live exit (2026-10-30), driven in the window: two workspaces added through the form; three requests in them reached the approve checkpoint with plan artifacts, three plan turns on gpt-5-mini; a comment on the `subtract` plan (add a docstring, rename the test) came back in the next plan; `multiply` was stopped and its VM went away; the app was quit with the stack kept running and reopened, and both other jobs were still at approve; `divide` was then approved, ran its build turn, and reached review with its artifact. The owner then moved the views from a floor and an inbox to a Jobs page and a job page, after GitHub Actions and wipp (2026-10-30): the Jobs page groups waiting for you, in progress and finished, with a workspace filter and search; the job page shows the badges, a waiting panel with the artifact it judges, and the pipeline as steps whose states come from `bastion_core::steps`; workspaces moved to Settings. Checked in the window on the live jobs. |"," | A4 | done | The diff, captured from the VM after each build and shown per file with line comments (e5da6d7). The checkpoint dial: ask, hold and auto, review never below hold, holds resumed after a restart (0bdb745). Turn guide and uncommitted-work flag (4b46dca). Landing fixes: the bundle names the branch, a failed land waits on the owner with its VM, and the land passes `target_branch` (75adbe2, f2898c6). 24 core tests, 29 app tests. Live exit (2026-10-31), driven in the window: on `divide`, line comments on `calc.py:5` and `test_calc.py:3` came back verbatim and each next diff answered them; on `subtract`, the owner approved the plan and the review, the land failed once on `target_checked_out_dirty` (an untracked `__pycache__` in the target) and waited, and Approve retried it: `demo-a` main got `0e30e2f`, both tests pass, and the VM is gone. Not run live: a hold expiring (30 min); the core and loop tests cover it. |","-| A5 | in progress | Spike N8 passes: a hook denies, holds and releases a call (e7fb375). `mise.toml` pins Rust 1.97 so local checks match CI (c8c6518). Step 1, the rules in `bastion-core`: constraint and capability ladders, the gate, and the audit chain (def679b). Steps 2 and 3: the governance tables with the owner's defaults seeded once, and the `pre-trigger` hook judged by the gate, with holds and audit records written by one task off the hook's path (a509bb1). Step 4: held calls on the job page (allow once, or refuse with a note), and a Governance page with the constraints and grants on their ladders and the audit chain verified as it is read. 37 core tests, 39 app tests. Next: the live exit. Not yet built: charter-sourced constraints, repository hooks, audit export, and the audit timeout test. |","+| A5 | in progress | Spike N8 passes: a hook denies, holds and releases a call (e7fb375). `mise.toml` pins Rust 1.97 so local checks match CI (c8c6518). Step 1, the rules in `bastion-core`: constraint and capability ladders, the gate, and the audit chain (def679b). Steps 2 and 3: the governance tables with the owner's defaults seeded once, and the `pre-trigger` hook judged by the gate, with holds and audit records written by one task off the hook's path (a509bb1). Step 4: held calls on the job page (allow once, or refuse with a note), and a Governance page with the constraints and grants on their ladders and the audit chain verified as it is read. 38 core tests, 39 app tests. Live exit (2026-10-31), driven in the window on `j4825765c` in `demo-a`: the plan turn's `sandbox::fs::write` to `PLAN.txt` waited on the job page; Allow once ran exactly that write in the VM, and the next write (`RISKS.txt`) waited again; Refuse with a note reached the agent, which put the risks in its reply instead. `keep-tests` at checked let `git -C /work/repo rm -n test_calc.py` through with `flagged: keep-tests` (audit entry 39); promoted to enforced (entry 40), the same call was refused with the rule's reason (entry 41). The Governance page verified all 41 entries, reported \"entry 20 does not follow\" after one byte of entry 20 was changed in the database, and verified again once it was restored. Still to build before A5 closes: charter-sourced constraints, repository hooks, audit export, and the audit timeout test. |"," | A6 to A13 | — | — |"," | Later (§10) | on hold | — |"," "]},{"oldStart":729,"oldLines":3,"newStart":729,"newLines":22,"lines":["   could not."," - `bastion-core` takes `sha2` for the audit chain. The hash is part of the","   rule, so it stays pure and tested with the rest (D19 updated).","+- The first rule matched a plain substring, so `keep-tests` (\"git rm\") never","+  bound `git -C /work/repo rm`. A rule's words now bind in order with any","+  words between them (`mentions` in `bastion-core`).","+- A rule on a command line cannot see a deleted test. One build rewrote","+  `test_calc.py` with `sandbox::fs::write` and dropped `test_add`, and no rule","+  bound that call; the owner caught it in the diff. Keeping tests needs a rule","+  on the diff at review, not on a call.","+- A refusal at plan does not carry into build. The owner refused `RISKS.txt`","+  at plan, and the build wrote it anyway, because writes are allowed at build.","+- A closed page's push handler read its disposed `StoredValue` and panicked,","+  so open pages stopped updating on push. `ipc::listen` now stops a handler","+  when its page closes.","+- Not fixed: typing a comma into the review note box while a wide diff is on","+  the page spins the webview at 100% CPU. The same comma in the Jobs search","+  box is fine. The page also scrolls sideways at review, so a layout loop is","+  the first suspect.","+- `iii-sandbox` passes the shell's whole environment, secrets included, into","+  worker VMs such as `opengantry` as `--env` flags. A9 starts the stack with","+  only the variables it needs."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"447b03f4-4e18-4cc4-b213-b73f26d87608","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":4,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":fal