{"parentUuid":"e5d729f1-9df7-46c2-a21e-962884ed7cb8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaYUXNTM9i731M3Vt75w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":380,"cache_read_input_tokens":475763,"output_tokens":1018,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":43},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":380,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1018,"cache_read_input_tokens":475763,"cache_creation_input_tokens":380,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":380},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"28331664-ccdc-4327-8b3c-8457aac25a6e","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgaYUWzcu2DarSxEDvfHr","type":"assistant","uuid":"b9e71d45-f8b3-4680-99e6-b58b37cc5319","timestamp":"2026-10-31T15:22:21.633Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"pure-pondering-goose"}
{"parentUuid":"b9e71d45-f8b3-4680-99e6-b58b37cc5319","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaYUXNTM9i731M3Vt75w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four A5 exit checks passed live, in the window on job `j4825765c` in `demo-a`. A5 stays open: charter-sourced constraints, repository hooks, audit export and the audit timeout test aren't built yet. CI passed on every A5 push through `b4f2704`; the run for the latest push, `ee4435e`, is still queued.\n\n**Exit checks:**\n1. **A write outside the grant waits:** the plan turn's `sandbox::fs::write` to `PLAN.txt` showed on the job page as held.\n2. **\"Allow once\" covers one call:** it ran exactly that write in the VM, and the next write (`RISKS.txt`) was held again. I refused that one with a note, and the agent put the risks in its reply instead.\n3. **Promotion changes the decision:** the same call, `git -C /work/repo rm -n test_calc.py`, passed with a `keep-tests` flag at checked (audit entry 39). After I promoted the rule to enforced (entry 40), the call was refused with the rule's reason (entry 41).\n4. **The audit is tamper-evident:** the Governance page verified all 41 entries. When I changed one byte of entry 20 in the database, it reported \"entry 20 does not follow from the one before it\". After I restored the byte, it verified again.\n\n**Two bugs found and fixed (`ee4435e`):**\n- **Rules never matched:** a rule matched a plain substring, so `keep-tests` (\"git rm\") could never match `git -C /work/repo rm`. A rule's words now match in order, with any words between them.\n- **Pages stopped updating:** the handler from a page I had already left crashed when an update arrived, and open pages then stopped updating by themselves. Handlers now stop when their page closes.\n\n**Found, not fixed:**\n- **A deleted test went through:** one build rewrote `test_calc.py` and dropped `test_add`, and no rule caught it, because rules only see command lines. I caught it in the diff and sent it back, and the next build restored it. Keeping tests needs a rule that checks the diff at review.\n- **A plan-stage refusal doesn't carry over:** I refused the `RISKS.txt` write at plan, and the build wrote it anyway, because writes are allowed at build.\n- **The view freezes on a comma:** typing a comma in the review note box, while a wide diff is on the page, sends the webview to 100% CPU. I reproduced it twice. A comma in the Jobs search box is fine. My first guess is a layout loop, because the review page also scrolls sideways. I haven't confirmed it.\n- **The view is behind:** Trunk hasn't rebuilt the view since 10:15, so the Governance page still uses the old wording (\"containing\" instead of \"with the words\").\n\nThe test job `j4825765c` is still waiting at review. I didn't land it.\n\nThe `PLAN.md` progress row now holds the exit evidence, and these findings are recorded under \"What A5 found so far\"."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":380,"cache_read_input_tokens":475763,"output_tokens":1018,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":43},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":380,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1018,"cache_read_input_tokens":475763,"cache_creation_input_tokens":380,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":380},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"28331664-ccdc-4327-8b3c-8457aac25a6e","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgaYUWzcu2DarSxEDvfHr","type":"assistant","uuid":"9b6005b6-9425-4c89-a218-1543ee586323","timestamp":"2026-10-31T15:22:23.766Z","advisorModel":"claude-